# Plots live with the data

**Incident (2026-08-27):** I/M, prior, and RT overlays for Stage B ablations
were written to repo `figs/modeling_details_ablations_bps20/`. User had to
ask them moved into the alyx/openalyx **model run dirs**. Wrong.

## Rule

Save figures **in the same ONE/alyx folder as the source**. Per-run fit
diagnostics go **inside that run directory**. Do **not** use repo `figs/`,
`output/`, or a new tree under the git checkout.

| Source | Put plots here |
|--------|----------------|
| `weights_run_*/` JSON | that same `weights_run_*/` |
| baseline Stage B (openalyx `models/`) | that openalyx run dir |
| ablations in alyx `models/new/` | that `models/new/` run dir |
| BWM `manifold/res`, FDR, tables | that analysis output dir on alyx |
| sim `manifold_sim/` | that experiment dir |

Shared diagnostics for one “best” model (e.g. RT vs data) go **in that
model’s run dir**, not a repo `figs/` sidecar.

Journals may **link** those ONE paths. They are not a place to dump
binaries.

`--out-root` / `save_dir` / `OUT=` must resolve to the data/model folder.
Defaulting to `figs/` because `plot_best_fit_results.py` once did is
still wrong.
